Feature: The end of a mission
  After the last item, a plane flies home in [[RTL]]. But if the mission ends with a loiter
  or a landing, the plane does that. A copter circles at the last waypoint, and a rover
  stays where it is.

  Expectation: Each waypoint reached moves the mission on
    Given the plane is flying the mission
    When the plane reaches a waypoint
    Then the vehicle's current item goes up by 1

  Expectation: After the last waypoint the plane flies home
    Given the plane is flying the mission
    And the last plan item is WAYPOINT
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the plane reaches the last item
    Then the autopilot mode is RTL
    And the plane is flying home

  Expectation: A mission that ends with a loiter keeps circling
    Given the plane is flying the mission
    And the last plan item is LOITER_UNLIM or LOITER_TURNS
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the plane reaches the last item
    Then the autopilot mode is AUTO
    And the plane is loitering

  Expectation: A mission that ends with a landing lands
    Given the plane is flying the mission
    And the last plan item is LAND
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the plane reaches the last item
    Then the plane is on the ground

  Expectation: A mission that ends with RTL flies home in AUTO
    Given the plane is flying the mission
    And the last plan item is RTL
    And the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the plane reaches the last item
    Then the autopilot mode is AUTO
    And the plane is flying home
